{"content":[{"c":["HOUSE OF THE ARCHIVES*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Building used for storage of records, annals, and decrees; a common structure in Near Eastern nations in the second millennium ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.5.17-6.1","r":"Ezra.5.17-6.1","rawR":"Ezra.5.17-6.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.5.17-6.1","value":"Ezra.5.17-6.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 5:17–6:1"},"). In the archives at Ecbatana, a summer resort for Persian kings, King Darius (521–486 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},") found an edict of Cyrus (559–530 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},") that entitled the Jews to begin reconstruction of the Jerusalem temple following the exile (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.6.2","r":"Ezra.6.2","rawR":"Ezra.6.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.6.2","value":"Ezra.6.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 6:2"},"). On the basis of that edict, Darius gave his support to renewed reconstruction efforts, which had been halted for 16 years due to local opposition (cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Hagg.1.1","r":"Hagg.1.1","rawR":"Hagg.1.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Hagg.1.1","value":"Hagg.1.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Hg 1:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Zech.1.1","r":"Zech.1.1","rawR":"Zech.1.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Zech.1.1","value":"Zech.1.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Zec 1:1"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"HouseoftheArchives","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ezr 5:17–6:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.5.17-6.1","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.5.17-6.1","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.5.17-6.1"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 6:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.6.2","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.6.2","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.6.2"},{"anchorText":"Hg 1:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Hagg.1.1","rawQueryValue":"Hagg.1.1","sourceRefExact":"Hagg.1.1"},{"anchorText":"Zec 1:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Zech.1.1","rawQueryValue":"Zech.1.1","sourceRefExact":"Zech.1.1"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"59b8036974f5b24278242dce2bf60a7522ac7262b0e59f9dcf413befdf0b6b4f","sourceItemName":"HouseoftheArchives","sourceItemOrder":378,"sourceMember":"Articles/H.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"HouseoftheArchives","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"House of the Archives*","title":"House of the Archives*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}